You do not need to change anything in your existing dbt models when switching to use SQL-inf – they will all work the same as before – but you now have the ability to use SQL-inf commands as native SQL functions.

Infer supports a number of SQL-inf commands, including `PREDICT`, `EXPLAIN`, `CLUSTER`, `SIMILAR_TO`, `TOPICS`, `SENTIMENT`. You can read more about SQL-inf and the commands it supports in the [SQL-inf Reference Guide](https://docs.getinfer.io/docs/category/commands).

